<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
 =============================================================================
  backup_rules.xml  |  Auto Backup rules for Android 11 and below (API <= 30)
 =============================================================================

  WHAT AUTO BACKUP DOES
  =====================
  When `android:allowBackup="true"`, Android periodically uploads the app's
  private data (SharedPreferences, files, databases) to the user's Google Drive
  and restores it when they install the app on a new device.

  WHY YOU MUST THINK ABOUT THIS DELIBERATELY
  ==========================================
  Auto Backup is opt-OUT, not opt-in. Anything not explicitly excluded leaves
  the device. Access tokens, session cookies, cached personal data and device
  identifiers must all be excluded, or they end up in cloud storage - and a
  restored stale token is a genuine security problem, not just a nuisance.

  CURRENT STATE
  =============
  This application stores no data at all yet, so no exclusions are required.
  The file exists, referenced and documented, so that the rules are added at the
  moment persistence is introduced rather than discovered missing later.

  HOW TO ADD AN EXCLUSION
  =======================
      <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="secure_session.xml" />
      <exclude domain="database"   path="credentials.db" />

  Valid domains: sharedpref, database, file, external, root.
  Companion file for API 31+: xml/data_extraction_rules.xml.
 =============================================================================
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <!-- No exclusions required: the application currently persists no data. -->
</full-backup-content>
